[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) holds every report about a wrong date since April. The desk merged them on
subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and the subjects all say the
same thing: wrong day. Read by tenant and by what the dates did, the reports hold separate problems.
Each one now has a ticket of its own.

<Callout kind="warn">
Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October. That closed two of its problems: <code>parser</code> is fixed, and
<code>hint</code> is won't fix because the booking-v3 form is retired. The one-day move is still open: no fix
named it, and closing #4471 does not close it.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  tickets={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/bskertchly/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/bskertchly/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2',
    'one-day move': 'https://github.com/bskertchly/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3',
  }}
/>

### parser: the shared parser reads dates month first

Every tenant on file writes dates day first. The shared parser reads them month first, so a booking
for 7 April lands on 4 July. This is the bug #4471 names. **Fixed** by engineering
(`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`), and the ticket is closed.
[Ticket](https://github.com/bskertchly/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).

### hint: the booking-v3 form shows the wrong order

The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, then reads what people type in the
tenant's day-first order. People do what the hint says, and the date flips before the parser sees
it. The result looks the same as the parser bug, but the parser fix does not touch it. **Won't fix**:
engineering retired the booking-v3 form, and the ticket is closed.
[Ticket](https://github.com/bskertchly/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

### one-day move: the date moves by one day

Some reports are not a swap. The date moves by one day: Tuesday 12 May shows as Monday 11 May, a
client in Lisbon gets Tuesday and a client in Toronto gets Monday, and one tenant sees it only in
June. That points at time zones or daylight saving, not date order. The desk had already noted these
reports (`desk-notes.json`), but the table on #4471 counts them under `parser`. **Open**: the parser fix does not
change time zones, so expect these reports to keep coming after #4471 closed.
[Ticket](https://github.com/bskertchly/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3).

## How the counts are made

The table above runs the kb's own cause logic (`causes.ts`) over the ticket export at render time,
one report per id, then takes the desk's one-day moves out of the cause their tenant puts them in.
For comparison, this is the table on #4471:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Intake tags (`parser`, `hint`) come from the reporter's browser and disagree with the cause in
both groups. Count by tenant, not by tag.

## For the desk

- Merging on subject put separate problems in one ticket. Before you mark a big ticket known, run it
  through the causes and read the reports that do not fit.
- When a merged ticket closes, check each problem in it. #4471 closed with the one-day move still open.

